  "id": "COMPOUND:30640 - PROTEIN:5782",
  "verbalization": "Alpneumine H is implicated in the biological activity of DMS-273 through a series of target relationships that converge on the mitochondrial thioredoxin protein. This pathway is supported by multiple evidence chains, each linking Alpneumine H to a different compound that ultimately targets DMS-273. The shared target of thioredoxin, mitochondrial across these pathways suggests a common mechanism of action, possibly involving redox regulation or oxidative stress modulation. The presence of multiple distinct compounds acting as intermediaries highlights the complexity of the interaction network, yet all converge on the same cellular target. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of thioredoxin in mediating the effects of Alpneumine H, potentially through a redox-dependent mechanism. The evidence supports a mechanism where Alpneumine H influences cellular processes via thioredoxin, which in turn modulates the activity of DMS-273, suggesting a broader role for thioredoxin in the biological response to Alpneumine H.",
